{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"The direct K expansion is faster for small token counts but slightly slower once the batch contains about 1,000 tokens, so I’ll keep it only in the range where it wins and retain the already-verified path above that threshold. Before the final verifier run, I’m also measuring whether a single combined projection GEMM is both bit-identical and faster at the larger token counts; I’ll only adopt it for shapes where both conditions hold."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, statistics, torch, reference\nshapes=[]\nfor line in open('workload.jsonl'):\n a=json.loads(line)['axes']; pair=(a['batch_size'],a['seq_len'])\n if pair not in shapes: shapes.append(pair)\nfor B,S in shapes:\n x=reference.get_inputs({'batch_size':B,'seq_len':S},torch.device('cuda'));h,p,qw,kw,vw,ow,inv,c=x.values()\n def sep(): return h@qw.t(),h@kw.t(),h@vw.t()\n def one():\n  z=h@torch.cat((qw,kw,vw),0).t();return z[...,:1024],z[...,1024:1280],z[...,1280:]\n a=sep();z=one();exact=all(torch.equal(u,v) for u,v in zip(a,z));del a,z\n def bench(fn):\n  for _ in range(5): y=fn()\n  vals=[]\n  for _ in range(25):\n   st=torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True);en=torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True);st.record();y=fn();en.record();en.synchronize();vals.append(st.elapsed_time(en))\n  return statistics.median(vals)\n ts=bench(sep);to=bench(one)\n print(f'{B:2d} {S:4d} M={B*S:5d} exact={str(exact):5s} sep={ts:.4f} one={to:.4f} ratio={ts/to:.3f}')\n del x;torch.cuda.empty_cache()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
